  "body": "Found while fixing #1174.\n\n**What happens.** `fanuc-lathe.cps` opens every section that carries no `PARAM LiveTool` (no move states a C angle) with `G97 S<rpm> M03` - the WORK spindle. A Mill-family operation on a mill-turn whose path states no C (e.g. a live-tool face mill, or any op the rotary gate did not stamp) would therefore spin the work at the milling tool's rpm if its moves happen to pass the post's meridian check (`radiusOf`), and the workholding rpm limit (#1031) does not judge it (`spindle_law::turns` is false for it, and #1174 kept that).\n\nNot reproduced end to end: most milling paths leave the meridian and are refused by the post (\"milling work, not turning\"), so this may be latent. Needs a check: either such a section is always refused before posting, or it must be voiced as live-tool work (live spindle word, work held), or judged against the chuck limit.\n\n**Where.** `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` section open (the non-live branch), `crates/app/src/setup_workholding.rs` (`work_speed`).\n\nDone means: a mill-family op on a mill-turn without C either never posts a work-spindle `M03` at the milling tool's rpm (refused by name, or voiced as live tooling), pinned by a test; the decision recorded.\n",
